hey guys so this is part 2 covering  everything we learned about Dark Souls 2  at e3 click here to see the previous  video if you haven't already and use the  links in each description to sort of  navigate to different topics within this  video so at e3 there were class choices  for Dark Souls 2 just like Resort Dark  Souls at e3 2011 however traditional  character creation seems to have taken a  bit of a change as well you won't choose  the class system anymore at least from  the way I understand it but instead  you'll customize your character through  some tutorial sessions by the sounds of  things these will incorporate a variety  of questions maybe like would you prefer  to attack quickly or would you prefer to  take a lot of hits then the game selects  a class for you based on that play style  we didn't get to experience this  tutorial session so it remains to be  seen how this will work in practice it  might not even be a big deal so let's go  through the character archetypes that  were playable at e3 first up was the  sorcerer there's a few changes here  pressing l1 with the catalyst equipped  allows you to perform a faster standard  spell l2 does a slower more powerful  version of the spell close-quarters  fighting was apparently still difficult  although it looks like casters will have  a huge variety and depth to their spells  the P are in charge of one of the booths  emphasized that enhanced customization  would be possible even for the spells  you cast it looks like Fromm is trying  to make every playstyle more viable  since sorcery and bow builds felt really  tacked on and less viable in Dark Souls  1 so one interesting side note about the  sorcerer is that you see him using fire  sorcery it's not pyromancy which is done  with a pyromancy and it's sorcery which  uses a catalyst and for everyone who  follows the law as much as I do this is  a pretty big deal because fire sorcery  is apparently a lost art does this mean  that the game is a prequel set before  the fire sorcery was lost or doesn't  mean that the fire sorcery was just  rediscovered somehow impaired in mind  this is from software we're talking  about so I'm pretty sure they'll have an  explanation ready for us but what do you  think do you think this means it's a  prequel let me know another awesome  character was the dual swordsman not  just because of his glorious cloth  physics every weapon in each  seems to have a unique r1 and a unique  r2 holding triangle instead of dual hand  in your right hand weapon puts you into  sort of like a power stance from which  you can perform a unique attack parrying  doesn't seem to be an option anymore  with dual wielding at least with the  weapons he was using but at least this  means that there'll be a huge array of  combos open to anyone who actually  decides to do a wheel moving towards the  to more standard characters we have this  footage of a temple knight using a  halberd and a hand axe here you'll  notice that the chip damage from the  enemy assault seems to be much more  common it was also confirmed by the devs  that some of the shields used as  catalysts can be used as catalysts for  casting spells adding strength to the  sort of paladin archetype and the final  character we'll cover is the warrior  that we've seen so much of whose  gameplay is pretty standard the best  thing I can think of to talk over during  his footage is that you can now hold  three things in each hand so weapons  shields talismans sorcery catalysts all  that stuff three in each hand so this  offers more variety but remember that  you'll still be trying to keep your  equipment load in mind so you're not  going to overburden yourself now if  you're super observant you might have  noticed a few more changes to the core  gameplay mechanics so in terms of  movement rolling seems to have changed  in that if you have a lighter character  you actually roll faster which is  nothing new and further as well as well  as acquiring more invincibility frames  than a heavier character so the extra  invincibility frames is a cool change  although playtesters noticed that  invincibility frames were really  difficult to exploit in the demo I also  have a feeling from the gameplay that  there won't be categories like fast or  old medium roll and heavy roll anymore  from the gameplay it seems like the roll  speed and distance scales with the  character weight I could be wrong though  parrying is reportedly much the same at  this stage although one journalist  mentioned that he could knock enemies to  the ground with it perhaps that's also a  method of crowd control playtesters  mentioned that they had a really hard  time parrying which is interesting  because it's already fairly challenging  as well back stabs are where most of the  changes appear and that's good  considering back steps need a nerf in  both PvE and PvP firstly they're harder  to perform I mentioned earlier that  enemies pivot much faster and track your  much better secondly they're really  really dynamic this time around a series  of complex slashes take place with short  swords and some testers mentioned that  they picked up the enemy with their stab  and slammed him onto the ground  but now these different animations  actually matter because many play  testers were shocked to discover that  they could actually take damage while  performing the animation this is a big  change imagine what it will be like to  be broken out of that backstab animation  or to take damage during it it makes me  wonder if it's possible to cancel the  animation after delivering a few blows  bearing this in mind what you prefer to  choose a light weapon with a backstab  that does a series of slashes or a heavy  weapon that winds up towards a big  damage if you have the time to perform  the attack animations madam now and back  steps no longer seem to be the best way  to deal with groups of humanoid enemies  so I'm sure from will fix the  overpowered role they used to play  especially in PvP as well another thing  at the core of a Souls game is subtle  implicit clues Dark Souls tells its  story through item locations it tells  you where to go by prompting your  intuition and your attention to detail  can help you navigate the game world  even in the demo we got a glimpse of  this there's a fragile wall in one of  the areas that hides a shortcut and the  wall can be smashed open if you bait a  total Knight into hitting the wall or  Dodger throw an explosive at the right  moment in another interview with polygon  you return in mirror the game's director  mentioned that he was really excited  about the possibilities within the new  engine he said that the engine had more  potential for subtle expression so not  like facial expression but like the  little hints that exist within the  gameplay without giving too much away  the example he gave was representing an  off-screen enemy with the movement of  shadow I can't predict what other cool  little things they'll throw into the  game but considering that we're still  discovering new things about Dark Souls  now imagine what possibilities they'll  have within the new engine now as a  final note you remember that a few  people were worried that the character  was blocking 100% physical damage with  the torch in an earlier demo so here's  what happened when Rubicon attempted to  block the total Knights giant hammer  with the torch this time around Rubicon  was fighting the total knight and  attempted to block with the torch the  blow completely staggered his character  the total Knight then walked behind him  during the stagger animation  and smacked his back into the ground I  think they fixed it guys a link to Road  Kahn's experience with the demo can be  found in the description so getting  towards the end now but I did save a lot  of the best to last interestingly  there's a few rumors of demon souls 2  coming out of e3 not dark souls 2 demon  souls 2 if you remember Sony actually  owns the rights to Demon Souls and the  head of Sony Studios recently came out  and proclaimed his love of Demon Souls  and there's a few other accounts coming  out of e3 where PR guys hinted at the  possibility that Demon Souls 2 exists  I'm not saying this means anything but  there's been enough accounts for me to  actually mention it so but yeah I think  it would be a really clever move on Sony  spot to actually make use of the Demon  Souls I paid that they own especially  with the ps4 coming out later in the  year can you imagine if we had to sort  of separate Souls games being developed  alongside each other I think that'd be  great and I'm really trying to hold back  my excitement here I don't want to get  too hyper to something that might not  even happen anyway the PC version of  Dark Souls 2 is reportedly looking miles  better than the ps3 version which makes  a lot of sense considering the  generational gap oh and after e3 I  mentioned in my earlier video a steam  logo appeared on the Dark Souls website  right after a three please tell me we  don't have to deal with another games  for Windows Live again so thanks for  watching guys like if you liked it and  check out the other Souls news videos in  this series cheers guys and thanks for  subscribing there's a lot more content  on the way and I can't wait to show you
 

